Article 2 (Duties)
The Committee shall perform the following duties:
1. Providing advice on the formulation of policies and improvement of systems relating to rehabilitation and bankruptcy proceedings;
2. Deliberating on and advising about standards for the establishment, composition and operation of custodial committees;
3. Deliberating on and advising about standards and procedures for selecting, managing, appointing and commissioning candidates for custodial committee members, custodians, examiners, bankruptcy trustees and rehabilitation commissioners (excluding rehabilitation commissioners under Article 601 (1) 2 of the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act), etc.;
4. Conducting overall evaluations of the work performed by custodial committee members and other persons specified in subparagraph 3, and providing advice thereon;
5. Other duties necessary for the systematic and uniform operation of rehabilitation and bankruptcy proceedings.
